# specX — agents must use skills (not improvisation)

This project uses **specX Spec-Driven Development**. Generic agile or "write a spec" behavior is wrong.

## Mandatory first read

1. `.cursor/skills/specx-sdd/SKILL.md`
2. `.cursor/skills/specx-sdd/reference.md` — OpenSpec, BMAD, Kiro, GSD, Ralph, Spec Kit DNA
3. `.cursor/skills/specx-graph/SKILL.md` — wikilinks, frontmatter, `## Graph` (Obsidian + agent navigation)
4. `specx/SPECX.md`
5. `specx/GRAPH.md` + `specx/Home.md`
6. `specx/foundation/STEERING.md`
7. `.specx/registry.yaml`

## Workflow skills (full process — read entire SKILL.md)

| Intent | Skill | Extra detail |
|--------|-------|----------------|
| Discovery | `specx-discover` | `phases.md` — lens per phase |
| Graph / links | `specx-graph` | Wikilinks on every artifact |
| Draft | `specx-specialist` | Named persona + `## Graph` |
| Challenge | `specx-critic` | Verdict required |
| Approve phase | `specx-approve` | Human said yes only |
| Revise | `specx-revise` | |
| New feature | `specx-propose` | Capabilities = OpenSpec |
| Requirements | `specx-spec` | ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED |
| Design | `specx-design` | ADR traceability |
| Tasks | `specx-tasks` | One checkbox = one session |
| Code | `specx-build` | Fresh context |
| Verify | `specx-verify` | Ralph loop until READY |
| Archive | `specx-archive` | Living specs merge |

Slash commands and `.specx/commands/` mirror these skills — **skills are authoritative**.

## Non-negotiables

- Dual-agent: Specialist + Critic before human gate
- **Linked markdown:** wikilinks + `## Graph` + frontmatter (`specx-graph`); maintain [[Home]]
- Git commits after approvals (git is memory)
- No code before spec reviewed (Kiro)
- Delta specs only during changes (OpenSpec)
- Product language in requirements; implementation in design/tasks
